commenti.body:
I'm the exact same way. The filmmakers spent untold hours creating their work, the least I can do is put my phone down and respect their effort. Then you watch one of these mini-series and so much is repeated that it is VERY obvious that the filmmakers didn't expect anyone to pay close attention.

&#x200B;

What's worse is, like you said, often these shows have a great premise or subject matter, but the constant re-treading over information for the sake of padding out the runtime makes them nigh unwatchable. I can't tell you how often I've come across something on streaming, being intrigued and then immediately retreating once I find out its 10 episodes long
